--   One Prop. 11 level as IL code, any fixed unit coefficients (bit data)
-- statement:
--   **One Prop. 11 level as IL code, any fixed unit coefficients (bit data).** For a fixed circuit over `ZMod 2` whose frame changes have `0/1` permutation parts and whose Lemma 10 shifts have coefficients `±k·d⁻¹` with `k, d ≤ D` prime to `N`, there is a constant `K` (depending on the circuit and `D`) such that for all sizes the level is an IL statement calling the child procedures, computing `levelR`, with cost `K · (V + 1) · (Bb + 2)² + rankSum C · (c₀ + 2)`.
